## The fixes

**1. Projected globals erased before the caller runs** — [prelude.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:96): `clj/run-main` no longer clears `clj.rt/globals`; the namespace lives for the task, like `globalThis` under `js/run-main`. The semantics are now one deliberate binding: the [:clojure profile](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/test/yang/call/conformance.clj:154) projects only via `clj/define-global!` (the duplicate `yin/def` task-store binding is gone), and [lower-unit](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2804) takes the projected exports so free reads publish through `clj/global-get`. A caller top-level definition publishes after the projection and shadows it; lexically bound names still win over both. Documented in the prelude ns docstring and [publish-to-globals](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2711).

**2. Source map `{:type :cell-ref}` dereferenced as a cell** — [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1203): routing and admission now require the authentic reference shape (`:type :cell-ref` plus the issued `:id` and `:seal`) before any `cell/get`. A source map carries neither, falls to the witness branch / invoker, and invokes as ordinary map data. A forged full shape still reaches `cell/get` and the VM seal refuses it — admission is not weakened.

**3. `js/kind-of` misclassified cell-backed foreign functions** — [prelude.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:135): the cell branch now consults `yang.call/eligible?` after the `:js/type` function/symbol checks, so a Python/PHP function cell is `:function`, while plain JS objects stay `:object`.

Boundaries held: no `yin/vm/**`, no `yang/core/call.cljc`, no evidence/narrative files.

## Regressions (in [cross_lang_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj:122))

Four new matrix legs: projection read through the runtime globals inside the caller's run, a second `clj/run-main` entry reading an earlier unit's global (`42`), caller shadowing of a projected name (`21`, caller's `+1` not donor's `+100`), the `{:type :cell-ref :marker 42}` map invocation returning `42n` to TypeScript, and `typeof py_fn` logging `"function"`.

Each was observed failing before the fix: `:clj/unbound` (projection erased), `Dead or forged cell reference {:effect :cell/get, :id nil}` (VM failure), and `typeof → object`.

